cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ICEtool, please cite it as below."
title: "ICEtool: a QGIS plugin to compute ground temperatures and quantify urban heat islands"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Evrard"
    given-names: "Arthur"
    affiliation: "Egis; INSA Toulouse"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Art-Ev/ICEtool"
url: "https://github.com/Art-Ev/ICEtool"
license: GPL-3.0
version: "2026.7.2"
keywords:
  - QGIS
  - urban heat island
  - UHI
  - ilot de chaleur urbain
  - ground temperature
  - urban planning
  - thermal resilience
abstract: >-
  ICEtool is an open-source QGIS plugin created and maintained by Arthur Evrard
  (engineer at Egis, lecturer at INSA Toulouse) to estimate ground temperatures
  in urban environments and quantify urban heat island effects. It originates
  from the "ICE" procedure developed within Egis & co-authored by Arthur.
  ICEtool is an applied-research project supported by Arthur, Egis and released 
  as open source with the academic backing of INSA Toulouse and sponsors (ADEME,
  Banque des Territoires, Region Nouvelle-Aquitaine...).